# TEBDLC Release Candidate — repository hygiene
# Jonathan Therrien, Marieville, Québec.
#
# Policy: ignore reproducible local artifacts and local/private environment state.
# Do NOT globally ignore evidence-oriented extensions: TEBDLC may intentionally
# persist logs, maps, binaries, archives, manifests or other material as proof.

# Python caches
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Local Python environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Reproducible build / packaging outputs
/build/
/dist/
*.egg-info/

# Explicitly local TEBDLC artifacts
/local-artifacts/

# Coverage / profiling generated locally
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
*.gcda
*.gcno
*.profraw
*.profdata

# IDE / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Temporary editor files
*.tmp
*.swp
*.bak
*~

# Local secrets and environment configuration
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local private key / certificate material
# Public test fixtures must live in an explicitly documented evidence/test path.
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# IMPORTANT TEBDLC EXCEPTIONS
# The following are intentionally NOT globally ignored:
#   *.log *.txt *.json *.out *.map *.so *.dll *.exe *.tar.gz
#   evidence/ docs/ vectors* FINGERPRINTS* RAW_RESULTS* manifest*
# A material artifact can become part of a falsification or proof bundle and
# must then remain versionable regardless of extension.
